# Art direction recognition

Player-visible sprites, icons, UI chrome, renderer presentation, palettes, pivots, atlases, and asset-pipeline tooling follow `.cursor/ART_DIRECTION_AND_ASSET_PIPELINE.md`.

When that work is in scope:

1. Use skill `rimworld-go-art-assets` (canonical playbook: `.cursor/skills/rimworld-go-art-assets/SKILL.md`).
2. Load only the spec sections that skill names for the asset family — not the whole file by default.
3. Keep pixels, texture handles, camera, and animation in presentation adapters; domain stays headless.
4. Never trace, extract, or reconstruct proprietary RimWorld art.
5. Do not bulk-produce assets until Wave 0 contracts and the §34 prototype gate are met.
6. Update matching ART wave checkboxes in the spec (`[x]` / `[-]` / `[!]`).

Skip the spec for headless simulation-only tasks with no visual output.
